2. General restrictions.
   Without prior written permission, you may not copy, distribute, transmit,
   display, modify, translate, create derivative works from, or make any commercial
   or non-commercial use of the Work, in whole or in part.

3. No AI use.
   Without prior written permission, the following are prohibited, whether done by
   a person or through an artificial intelligence system, machine-learning model,
   large language model, coding agent, crawler, scraper or any other automated
   means:
   (a) using the Work to train, pre-train, fine-tune, align, evaluate or benchmark
       any AI model;
   (b) adding the Work to any dataset, corpus, embedding store, vector database or
       retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) index;
   (c) using AI to analyze the Work's code, screens, features or flows (including
       reverse engineering and "REA" analysis) in order to copy, reconstruct,
       imitate, re-implement, translate or convert it;
   (d) supplying the Work as a prompt or reference to generate substantially
       similar code, designs or products;
   (e) collecting the Work by crawling, scraping, or text and data mining.

4. Text and data mining reservation.
   Pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790 and any other law that
   recognizes such a reservation, the rights holder expressly reserves all text and
   data mining rights in the Work. This reservation is stated in plain language,
   readable by people and machines, in this document and at the top of the README.

5. GitHub Terms of Service.
   If this repository is public on GitHub, no use is permitted beyond what GitHub's
   Terms of Service require (viewing and forking within GitHub). A fork grants no
   other rights.

6. Third-party components.
   Third-party open-source code and materials included in this repository remain
